# Security fixes that Semgrep's own pins hold back: every Semgrep release up to 1.187.0 pins mcp==1.29.0 and
# wcmatch~=8.3. `make requirements` writes these into semgrep.txt in place of Semgrep's choice, with their hashes, and
# the sast job installs that lock with --no-deps so pip does not put Semgrep's pins back. Semgrep scans the same
# with them (same files scanned, same findings, the same --exclude matching). Drop a line once Semgrep allows it.
# GHSA-qx49-fqc8-xw99: the MCP SDK's OAuth client could send credentials to a server the MCP server chose.
mcp==1.30.0
# GHSA-53pm-wgxf-c6qf: polynomial-time ReDoS matching untrusted names against multi-star patterns.
wcmatch==11.2
